{"reference":"Genesis 6","book":"Genesis","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Creation and reversal","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A later prophetic passage sweeps through humans, animals, birds, and fish in a creation-scale judgment commonly read as creation reversal with flood resonances. That is a disputed interpretive connection: it can illuminate how later Scripture reuses creation language, but it does not erase the distinct narrative work of Genesis 6.","verse_refs":["Genesis 6:7"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_006_de2284c605d0e79ddcc8d223"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
